LIFE EMPIRE: ESPORTS TYCOON
Phone System & Player Career Expansion
Technical Product Requirements & Implementation Blueprint
Version: 1.0 Platform: React + TypeScript Web Game Development approach: Modular implementation, preserving existing game systems and save compatibility.
 
⸻
 
PART 1 — PRODUCT VISION
1.1 Objective
Transform Life Empire: Esports Tycoon from a traditional esports management simulator into a living esports-industry simulation.
Introduce an in-game smartphone that gives players access to the fictional esports ecosystem.
The phone should simulate:
* Esports community culture.
* Social media.
* Organisation rivalries.
* News and controversies.
* Personal finances.
* Investments.
* Player popularity.
* Content creation.
* Private communications.
* Professional esports careers.
The phone must not operate as an isolated collection of mini-applications.
Every application must receive information from the same simulated game world.
1.2 Two Starting Career Paths
The game must support two independent starting experiences.
CAREER A — ORGANISATION OWNER
The existing organisation-management experience.
The player:
* Creates an organisation.
* Chooses its name, country and identity.
* Recruits players.
* Hires staff.
* Manages salaries.
* Enters tournaments.
* Negotiates sponsorships.
* Develops the organisation.
* Competes internationally.
CAREER B — ESPORTS PLAYER
A completely new career experience.
The player:
* Creates an individual player identity.
* Selects a game and country.
* Starts as an amateur.
* Joins smaller teams.
* Participates in tryouts.
* Receives professional contracts.
* Builds popularity.
* Earns salary and sponsorships.
* Eventually becomes a superstar.
* Can retire and establish an esports organisation.
Both careers use the same world simulation, phone, economy, organisations, tournaments and social ecosystem.
 
